🩺 Breast Cancer Prediction using Machine Learning
This project provides a comprehensive pipeline for breast cancer classification using supervised machine learning models. It aims to accurately classify tumors as malignant or benign using medical diagnostic data.

📊 Dataset
The project uses the Breast Cancer Wisconsin (Diagnostic) Dataset, which includes:

569 samples

30 numeric features computed from a digitized image of a fine needle aspirate (FNA) of a breast mass

Binary target: 0 for malignant, 1 for benign

✅ Objectives
Preprocess and explore the dataset

Visualize patterns and correlations

Train and evaluate classification models

Determine the best performing model

Help assist early detection of breast cancer

